#
# Example-conformance cells for the semantic-topology slice. Each cell unions the module
# with the named fixture and validates it against the canonical GENERATED projections
# (generated/shapes/{validation-shapes,constraint-shapes,procedural-constraints}.ttl) under
# the native Rust conformance harness — the slice hand-authors NO shapes.ttl; the pipeline
# DERIVES the SHACL from the module's logic:Constraint gates and EL-safe OWL cardinality
# restrictions. gmeow:exampleFile is SLICE-RELATIVE; gmeow:expectedViolationCode is the
# COARSE native finding code finding_from_shacl builds as
# "shacl.<ConstraintComponentLocalName>". Almost every slice gate is a logic:Constraint
# (rejecting with shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent); the one exception is the EL-safe
# owl:minQualifiedCardinality restriction on gmeow:CompilationPreservationRecord's
# logic:preservationKind, which rejects a kind-less record with
# shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent instead. The SPECIFIC slice failure class is named in
# gmeow:conformanceRationale, and each counter-example isolates exactly ONE violation
# (AND-NO-OTHER). The conformant worked example lives under examples/ and is exercised as a
# competency cqDataFile and the example sweep.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/semantic-topology/tests/> .

# === AC: every compilation records a correspondence ========================= #
ex:ecCompilationNoCorrespondence a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/compilation-no-correspondence.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:ComplexCompilation that records its preservation/loss judgment and carries its full standpoint/world/time context but records NO gmeow:CellSourceCorrespondence, so the ∀→∃(∧∧) SPARQL constraint of gmeow:CompilationMustRecordCorrespondence MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding. Every other required datum is present, isolating the missing correspondence." .

# === AC: a recorded correspondence must carry a genuine row (not be empty) == #
ex:ecCompilationCorrespondenceEmpty a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/compilation-correspondence-empty.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:ComplexCompilation that DOES record a gmeow:CellSourceCorrespondence (and records its preservation/loss judgment and carries its full standpoint/world/time context) but the correspondence record carries ZERO gmeow:correspondenceCell rows, so no cell is traced to its evidence. The ∀→∃(∧∧) SPARQL constraint of gmeow:CompilationMustRecordCorrespondence MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding — an empty correspondence record is exactly as much a black box as a missing one." .

# === AC: every compilation records a preservation/loss judgment ============= #
ex:ecCompilationNoLossRecord a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/compilation-no-loss-record.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:ComplexCompilation that records its correspondence (with a genuine row, so gmeow:CompilationMustRecordCorrespondence is satisfied and NOT the violation under test) and carries its full standpoint/world/time context but records NO gmeow:CompilationPreservationRecord, so the ∀→∃ SPARQL constraint of gmeow:CompilationMustRecordLoss MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding. Every other required datum is present, isolating the missing preservation/loss record." .

# === AC: a preservation record must name a preservation kind (not be empty) = #
ex:ecCompilationPreservationNoKind a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/compilation-preservation-no-kind.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:ComplexCompilation with a valid correspondence (with a row) and full standpoint/world/time context that DOES record a gmeow:CompilationPreservationRecord — but that record names NO logic:preservationKind at all. The EL-safe owl:minQualifiedCardinality 1 restriction on logic:preservationKind (owl:onClass logic:PreservationKind) MUST reject it with shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding: with no preservationKind bound, gmeow:CompilationPreservationBoundaryConstraint's existential guard never fires, so this is the sole violation — a hollow ledger entry is closed exactly like a missing one." .

# === AC: a lossy/unsupported preservation kind must name its boundary ======= #
ex:ecCompilationPreservationLossyNoBoundary a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/compilation-preservation-lossy-no-boundary.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:ComplexCompilation with a valid correspondence and full standpoint/world/time context whose gmeow:CompilationPreservationRecord carries EXACTLY ONE logic:preservationKind (logic:SoundUnderApproximation, satisfying the cardinality restriction and NOT the violation under test) but names NO logic:expressivenessBoundary. The ∀→∃ SPARQL constraint of gmeow:CompilationPreservationBoundaryConstraint MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding: a lossy preservation judgment naming no boundary is the honesty gap Principle 17 forbids." .

# === A compilation carries its standpoint/world/time context ================ #
ex:ecCompilationNoStandpointContext a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/compilation-no-standpoint-context.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:ComplexCompilation that records its correspondence and preservation/loss judgment and carries its possible-world and time-scope context but omits its gmeow:compilationStandpoint, so the ∀→(∃∧∃∧∃) SPARQL constraint of gmeow:CompilationContextConstraint MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (gmeow:CompilationMissingContext). Every other required datum is present, isolating the missing standpoint." .

# === The governing invariant: no raw result asserted as global truth ======== #
ex:ecTopologyResultAssertedGlobalTruth a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/topology-result-asserted-as-global-truth.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:TopologyComputation that asserts a global truth (gmeow:assertsGlobalTruth true) with no gmeow:TopologyClaim that gmeow:claimForComputation it, gmeow:extendsToGlobalSection, and gmeow:dischargesObstruction, so the ∀→∃(join) SPARQL constraint of gmeow:AssertedTopologyResultConstraint MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding. gmeow:producesResult points at a gmeow:TopologyResult wrapper, so the undischarged global-truth assertion is the sole violation — a computed feature is a math:LocalSection, never automatically a global truth." .

# === The governing invariant: the discharge witness must be a typed claim === #
ex:ecTopologyClaimDischargeNotTyped a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/topology-claim-discharge-not-typed.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:TopologyComputation asserting a global truth whose gmeow:producesResult correctly points at a gmeow:TopologyResult wrapper (NOT the violation under test), and a resource that carries every discharge EDGE (gmeow:claimForComputation, gmeow:dischargesObstruction, gmeow:extendsToGlobalSection) but is never asserted rdf:type gmeow:TopologyClaim. The ∀→∃(join) SPARQL constraint of gmeow:AssertedTopologyResultConstraint now requires the discharge witness be TYPED gmeow:TopologyClaim, so it MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding — any resource carrying three predicates is not a discharging claim." .

# === A topology claim carries an attributed status ========================== #
ex:ecTopologyClaimNoAttributedStatus a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/topology-claim-no-attributed-status.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:TopologyClaim carrying its inherited gmeow:observationMethod (satisfying the gmeow:StandpointClaim exactly-one obligation, so that is NOT the violation) and its result but carrying NO gmeow:vantage attribution, so the ∀→∃ SPARQL constraint of gmeow:TopologyClaimStatusConstraint MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (gmeow:TopologyClaimMissingStatus). The anonymous, unattributed claim is the sole violation." .

# === a computation result must not be conflated with a raw math: object ===== #
ex:ecComputationResultConflated a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/computation-result-conflated-with-math-object.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:TopologyComputation whose gmeow:producesResult value is a raw math:PersistenceDiagram instead of a gmeow:TopologyResult wrapper, so the ∀→(∃∧¬∃) SPARQL constraint of gmeow:ResultObjectConflationConstraint (the result is not TYPED gmeow:TopologyResult, and it matches the math: namespace) MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (gmeow:ResultObjectConflation). The computation asserts no global truth, isolating the conflation." .

# === a computation result must be POSITIVELY typed gmeow:TopologyResult ===== #
ex:ecComputationResultUntyped a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/computation-result-untyped.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The counter-example declares a gmeow:TopologyComputation whose gmeow:producesResult value is a genuine, unrelated resource (gmeow:InformationObject) — never conflated with a raw math: object — but never asserted rdf:type gmeow:TopologyResult. The positive-existential arm of gmeow:ResultObjectConflationConstraint's ∀→(∃∧¬∃) SPARQL constraint MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (gmeow:ResultObjectConflation): the gmeow:TopologyResult wrapper type is positively required, not merely permitted, and an untyped result does not satisfy it." .

# NOTE: the conformant worked example (examples/compilation-worked.ttl) is exercised as the
# competency cqDataFile (merged, asserted lane) and by the example sweep — it is NOT
# registered as a "conforms" cell here because it references shared cross-slice grounding
# individuals (an observation method, a number system, the credence-derivation kind, the
# stability theorem, a severity, a preservation kind) that are typed only in their owning
# slices, exactly as the model-serving slice keeps its conformant demonstrators out of the
# example-conformance cells.
